The design synchronizes `sclk`, `mosi`, and `cs_n` with 2-stage synchronizers. A third register on `sclk` provides the previous value for rising-edge detection. All events are evaluated on the synchronized signals in the `clk` domain.

Since `mosi` and `sclk` are synchronized through the same number of stages, `mosi` is sampled at the same moment the `sclk` edge is detected. `mosi` is stable around the rising edge because the master holds it for half a period or more, and `clk` is at least 8x faster, so this is safe.

Reset clears `data`, `valid`, and the bit count. The `shift_reg` is also cleared on reset, which is harmless.

When `cs_n` is high, the bit count is cleared and `valid` is 0. The edge detector keeps tracking `sclk` through the idle state, so `sclk_prev` is still correct when `cs_n` falls.

Because `valid` is registered and set only in E3, it is high for one cycle. In every other case it is cleared.

