- Accepted operations are computed from the registered count, so `full` and `empty` are registered.
- A read and write in the same cycle are each accepted only if their own condition holds. When the FIFO is full, a write is ignored even if a read is accepted. When it is empty, a read is ignored even if a write is accepted.
- `rd_data` is registered and loaded from `mem[rd_ptr]` on an accepted read. Because a read is accepted only when the FIFO is non-empty, the entry being read was written in an earlier cycle.

