The design uses a 4-entry memory with 2-bit read and write pointers and a 3-bit count. Both the write and read acceptance conditions are computed from the registered `full` and `empty` flags, so a write while full and a read while empty are ignored.

When the FIFO is full and both `wr_en` and `rd_en` are set, the read is accepted and the write is ignored, so the count drops by one. When the FIFO is empty and both are set, the write is accepted and the read is ignored, so the count rises by one and `rd_data` is unchanged.

