I synchronize all three SPI inputs with 2-stage synchronizers. A third register stage on sclk gives rising-edge detection. Because mosi and sclk pass through the same number of stages, the sampled mosi stays aligned with the detected sclk edge.

Design details:
- `sclk_rise = sclk_s2 & ~sclk_s3`, evaluated in the clk domain.
- E1 (cs_n high) clears `bit_count` and `valid`. Because the synchronized cs_n is used, the count is re-aligned each time cs_n is seen high, so a falling edge always starts a fresh byte.
- The E1 condition also takes priority over a simultaneous sclk edge.
- E3 writes `data` from `{shift_reg[6:0], mosi_s2}` and sets `valid` for one cycle. The default assignment `valid <= 0` ensures the pulse is exactly one cycle wide.
- Latency from the 8th sclk rising edge to `valid` is about 3 clk cycles (2 synchronizer stages plus the register), which is within the 6-cycle limit.
- The synchronizer registers reset to values for the idle state (`cs_n` = 1, `sclk` = 0), so no false edge appears after reset.

```verilog
module spi_slave_rx (
    input  wire       clk,    // system clock
    input  wire       rst_n,  // active-low synchronous reset
    input  wire       sclk,   // SPI clock from master (asynchronous to clk)
    input  wire       mosi,   // master-out slave-in data
    input  wire       cs_n,   // active-low chip select
    output reg  [7:0] data,   // last complete byte received
    output reg        valid   // one-clk-cycle pulse when data is updated
);

    reg sclk_s1, sclk_s2, sclk_s3;
    reg mosi_s1, mosi_s2;
    reg cs_s1, cs_s2;

    reg [7:0] shift_reg;
    reg [2:0] bit_count;

    wire sclk_rise = sclk_s2 & ~sclk_s3;

    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (!rst_n) begin
            sclk_s1 <= 1'b0;
            sclk_s2 <= 1'b0;
            sclk_s3 <= 1'b0;
            mosi_s1 <= 1'b0;
            mosi_s2 <= 1'b0;
            cs_s1   <= 1'b1;
            cs_s2   <= 1'b1;
            bit_count <= 3'd0;
            shift_reg <= 8'd0;
            data      <= 8'd0;
            valid     <= 1'b0;
        end else begin
            sclk_s1 <= sclk;
            sclk_s2 <= sclk_s1;
            sclk_s3 <= sclk_s2;
            mosi_s1 <= mosi;
            mosi_s2 <= mosi_s1;
            cs_s1   <= cs_n;
            cs_s2   <= cs_s1;

            valid <= 1'b0;

            if (cs_s2) begin
                bit_count <= 3'd0;
            end else if (sclk_rise) begin
                if (bit_count != 3'd7) begin
                    shift_reg <= {shift_reg[6:0], mosi_s2};
                    bit_count <= bit_count + 3'd1;
                end else begin
                    data      <= {shift_reg[6:0], mosi_s2};
                    valid     <= 1'b1;
                    bit_count <= 3'd0;
                end
            end
        end
    end

endmodule
