Design notes: the FIFO uses a 4-entry memory, 2-bit read and write pointers, and a 3-bit count. Accepted reads and writes are computed from the current `full`/`empty` registers. When the FIFO is empty, a simultaneous read and write is not an issue because the read is ignored and only the write is accepted. When it is full, only the read is accepted.

