The design synchronizes all three SPI inputs with 2-stage synchronizers and detects `sclk` rising edges in the `clk` domain.

**Synchronization and edge detection**
- `sclk`, `mosi` and `cs_n` each pass through two flip-flops.
- `sclk` gets one extra register stage, so a rising edge is seen as `sclk_s2 & ~sclk_s3`.
- `mosi` uses the same synchronizer depth as `sclk`, so it is sampled at the matching delay.
- With f(clk) ≥ 8 × f(sclk), MOSI is still stable when the edge is detected, which gives correct mode‑0 sampling.

**Latency**
- `valid` rises 3 clk cycles after the 8th `sclk` rising edge (plus up to one cycle of sampling uncertainty), which is within the ≤ 6 requirement.

**Reset behaviour**
- On `rst_n = 0`, `bit_count`, `data`, `valid` and `shift_reg` are cleared.
- The `cs_n` synchronizer is reset to 1 (inactive), so the receiver stays idle while the `sclk` synchronizer settles.
- The `sclk` synchronizer is not reset. If it were cleared to 0 while `sclk` is high, the design could see a false rising edge right after reset.
- Keep `rst_n` low for at least 3 cycles. This lets the unreset synchronizer registers reach defined values.

**Event mapping**
- E1 (`cs_n` high, after synchronization) has priority. It clears `bit_count`, so the byte boundary re-aligns on every `cs_n` fall.
- E2 and E3 handle the shifting and byte completion.
- `valid` defaults to 0 every cycle, which gives the exact 1-cycle pulse.

```verilog
module spi_slave_rx (
    input  wire       clk,    // system clock
    input  wire       rst_n,  // active-low synchronous reset
    input  wire       sclk,   // SPI clock from master (asynchronous to clk)
    input  wire       mosi,   // master-out slave-in data
    input  wire       cs_n,   // active-low chip select
    output reg  [7:0] data,   // last complete byte received
    output reg        valid   // one-clk-cycle pulse when data is updated
);

    // Synchronizers
    reg sclk_s1, sclk_s2, sclk_s3;
    reg mosi_s1, mosi_s2;
    reg cs_s1,   cs_s2;

    reg [6:0] shift_reg;
    reg [2:0] bit_count;

    wire sclk_rise = sclk_s2 & ~sclk_s3;

    // sclk / mosi synchronizers (free-running)
    always @(posedge clk) begin
        sclk_s1 <= sclk;
        sclk_s2 <= sclk_s1;
        sclk_s3 <= sclk_s2;
        mosi_s1 <= mosi;
        mosi_s2 <= mosi_s1;
    end

    // cs_n synchronizer, reset to inactive
    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (!rst_n) begin
            cs_s1 <= 1'b1;
            cs_s2 <= 1'b1;
        end else begin
            cs_s1 <= cs_n;
            cs_s2 <= cs_s1;
        end
    end

    // Receive logic
    always @(posedge clk) begin
        if (!rst_n) begin
            bit_count <= 3'd0;
            shift_reg <= 7'd0;
            data      <= 8'd0;
            valid     <= 1'b0;
        end else begin
            valid <= 1'b0;
            if (cs_s2) begin
                bit_count <= 3'd0;
            end else if (sclk_rise) begin
                if (bit_count == 3'd7) begin
                    data      <= {shift_reg[6:0], mosi_s2};
                    valid     <= 1'b1;
                    bit_count <= 3'd0;
                end else begin
                    shift_reg <= {shift_reg[5:0], mosi_s2};
                    bit_count <= bit_count + 3'd1;
                end
            end
        end
    end

endmodule
